%[text] # Normalizing to Raman scatter when there is none
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"Table of Contents"}
%[text] ### Preface
%[text] **Scenario: You use a Horiba Aqualog and measure highly fluorescent samples.** Your Raman scan areas are likely quite low, right? Anything below ~1s integration time on an Aqualog may have this issue and it needs consideration. Unfortunately, this issue requires a non-standard workflow, but is possible to address **if** you have a nice Raman Scan (2D Emission).
%[text] What do do BEFORE you get here (but you can run this example of course!):
%[text] - Measure your EEMs as you would
%[text] - Per day, measure a Raman scan using the Aqualog's software feature.
%[text] - Export this scan using the HJY Export feature
%[text] - Copy the only "RSUNIT (01) - Emission Graph.dat" file as many times as your have samples.
%[text] - Rename the "RSUNIT (01) - Emission Graph.dat" copies to match the sample names (see the examples in the export folder). "RSUNIT (01) - Emission Graph.dat" becomes  "B08 (01) - Emission Graph.dat" and so on.
%[text] - Delete or rename the original "RSUNIT (01) - Emission Graph.dat"
%[text] - Make sure no other "Emission Graph.dat" files are there. They will cause trouble. \
%[text]  I am sorry for this additional workload. There are no better solutions. Contact
%[text] ### Setup
%[text] This section sets up your MATLAB environment so we can get going.
cd(fileparts(matlab.desktop.editor.getActiveFilename))
clearvars,clc
close all force
tbx=drEEMtoolbox;
%[text] ### Data Import
%[text] Before we get to the interesting bit, we need to import the data. You can import .dat files, but here, I chose to import from the opj file directly. Actually, to keep the toolbox size small, you can see how that import would look.
%[text] ```matlabCodeExample
%[text] [samples,blanks] = tbx.importaqualog(pwd);
%[text] ```
%[text] But instead, I will import the much smaller NetCDF file with some of the internal drEEM functions (don't worry, `importaqualog` would use these for you).
cd export
[samples,blanks] = horibaRawdata.convertTodrEEMdataset(horibaRawdata.importFromNetCDF('2024-07-11-measurements_minimal.nc')); %[output:77e49066]
%[text] Now it's time to impor the metadata:
samples=tbx.associatemetadata(samples,"scan_example_metadata.xlsx","sample_identifier"); %[output:5f032ad5]
%[text] Now comes the trick: Import the Raman scans
status=drEEMstatus(suppSpectraInfo='2D Emission scans (Raman Unit)');
scans=tbx.importscans('* - Emission Graph.dat',status,'axisColumn',1,spectrumColumn=14);
clearvars status
cd ..
%[text] ### Preparation
[samples,blanks,scans] = tbx.alignsamples(samples,blanks,scans); %[output:0c3e14bc]
blanks=tbx.mergemeasurements(blanks,scans,"supplementarySpectra");
clearvars scans
blanks = tbx.addcomment(blanks,'Moved 3D Raman scans (30s 1px binning) to suppSpectra since samples do not contain enough Raman scatter.');
%[text] ### Prepropcessing
samples=tbx.processabsorbance(samples, ... %[output:group:5bb9b31b] %[output:2c09717e]
    "correctBase",true,... %[output:2c09717e]
    "baseWave",600,... %[output:2c09717e]
    "extrapolate",true,... %[output:2c09717e]
    "zero",false,... %[output:2c09717e]
    plot=false); %[output:group:5bb9b31b] %[output:2c09717e]
samples=tbx.ifecorrection(samples,plot=false); %[output:89f65f60]
samples=tbx.subtractblanks(samples,blanks,plot=false);
load(fullfile('export','scatteroptions_scan_example.mat'))
samples=tbx.handlescatter(samples,scatteroptions);
clearvars scatteroptions
%[text] ### Normalization comparison
divider=samples.metadata.integration_time_scan./samples.metadata.integration_time_eem; 
multiplier=samples.metadata.binning_eem./samples.metadata.binning_scan; 

blanks.suppSpectra=blanks.suppSpectra./divider.*multiplier;
figure %[output:08066b49]
nexttile %[output:08066b49]
plot(blanks.suppSpectraAxis,blanks.suppSpectra(1,:),'k',DisplayName='2D Raman scan') %[output:08066b49]
hold on %[output:08066b49]
plot(blanks.Em,blanks.X(1,:,blanks.Ex==350),DisplayName='EEM Raman scan') %[output:08066b49]
legend %[output:08066b49]
title('Raman Scan comparison') %[output:08066b49]
xlim([340 500]) %[output:08066b49]
ylim([0 2000]) %[output:08066b49]

samples_eem=tbx.ramancalibration(samples,blanks,source="EEM",plot=false); %[output:6c0ebb25]
samples_scan=tbx.ramancalibration(samples,blanks,source="scan",plot=false);

eem_area=samples_eem.history(end).details.area;
scan_area=samples_scan.history(end).details.area;


nexttile %[output:08066b49]
plot(samples.Em,samples_scan.X(1,:,1),'k',DisplayName='2D Raman scan normalization') %[output:08066b49]
hold on %[output:08066b49]
plot(samples.Em,samples_eem.X(1,:,1),DisplayName='EEM Raman scan normalization') %[output:08066b49]

legend %[output:08066b49]
title('RU data comparison') %[output:08066b49]
disp(['Areas are within ',num2str(100-round(unique(eem_area)./unique(scan_area)*100,2)),' %']) %[output:324349a1]
samples=samples_scan;
clearvars -except samples tbx
disp('Example script finished.') %[output:3824ff20]

